  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - In the absence of a Noise Impact Assessment, Air Quality Assessment and details of a ventilation and extraction system, it has not been demonstrated that the Shisha Lounge, including the use of the rear extension with a retractable roof and late night opening hours, does not result in unacceptable levels of noise, disturbance, smoke and odour emission affecting the living conditions of the neighbouring occupiers at Nos. 251A, 253A and 255A Mitcham Lane and the rear gardens at No.86 Fallsbrook Road and Ethel Villa. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies LP2, LP14 and LP45 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023), Policies D13 and D14 of the London Plan (2021) and the National Planning Policy Framework (2024).",
    "Reason : 2 - The submitted Fire Safety Statement contains inaccuracies regrading the fire safety provisions within the premises, including reference to a mechanical extraction system for smoke control which has not been installed. As such, it has not been sufficiently demonstrated that the fire safety strategy has been prepared on the basis of accurate information and that fire safety has been adequately considered at the design stage. The proposal therefore fails to comply with Policy D12 of the London Plan (2024). ",
    "Reason : 3 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to make available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the principle of the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal.",
    "Reason : 4 - INFORMATIVE: The applicant is advised that the signage installed on the shopfront requires separate advertisement consent under the Town and Country Planning (Control of Advertisements) (England) Regulations. "
  ],
